According to the latest report from Intel Market Research, the global Postpartum Care and Rehabilitation market was valued at USD 9.09 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 19.17 billion by 2031, expanding at a significant CAGR of 11.4% during the forecast period (2025–2031). This growth trajectory reflects increasing global emphasis on maternal healthcare and the rising adoption of professional postnatal recovery services worldwide.
Understanding Postpartum Care and Rehabilitation
Postpartum care and rehabilitation encompasses comprehensive medical and wellness services designed to support women's physical and psychological recovery after childbirth. The sector has evolved beyond traditional postnatal care to include specialized rehabilitation programs addressing common postpartum complications such as diastasis recti, pelvic floor disorders, and perinatal mood disturbances.
Modern postpartum services typically integrate three key components:
•	Maternity center programs providing nutritional counseling and infant care support
•	Postpartum repair therapies targeting musculoskeletal rehabilitation
•	Confinement care services offering personalized nursing and emotional support
